=== guest page-table write-protection cost probe (in-VM, guest EL1, CNTVCT_EL0) ===
  payload 1716 bytes, RAM 64 MiB, 512 write-protected PT pages

=== 0. calibration ===
  CNTFRQ_EL0 24000000 Hz (41.67 ns/tick);  {isb;mrs cntvct} 9.21 ns;  empty loop 0.307 ns
  dependent ADD 0.3102 ns -> clock ~ 3.22 GHz  (cycle columns are +/-5%, modelled)
  rmap hash: (frame ^ (frame >> 5)) & 0x3ff, verified collision-free for 512 frames

=== 1. what ESR_EL1 tells the write-protect handler ===
  a LOAD from the write-protected page took 0 fault(s) and returned 0x0
  faults taken by the five stores: 5 (expected 5)

  STR  Xt, [Xn]      (8-byte store)
    ESR_EL1 = 0x000000009600004f   EC=0x25  ISV=0  SAS=0  SSE=0  SRT=0  SF=0  AR=0
    WnR=1  CM=0  S1PTW=0  DFSC=0x0f   FAR_EL1=0x400000000000
    ELR_EL1=0x4000019c  instruction word at ELR = 0xf9000005  (Rt field = 5)

  STRB Wt, [Xn]      (1-byte store)
    ESR_EL1 = 0x000000009600004f   EC=0x25  ISV=0  SAS=0  SSE=0  SRT=0  SF=0  AR=0
    WnR=1  CM=0  S1PTW=0  DFSC=0x0f   FAR_EL1=0x400000000000
    ELR_EL1=0x400001a0  instruction word at ELR = 0x39000005  (Rt field = 5)

  STR  Wt, [Xn]      (4-byte store)
    ESR_EL1 = 0x000000009600004f   EC=0x25  ISV=0  SAS=0  SSE=0  SRT=0  SF=0  AR=0
    WnR=1  CM=0  S1PTW=0  DFSC=0x0f   FAR_EL1=0x400000000000
    ELR_EL1=0x400001a4  instruction word at ELR = 0xb9000005  (Rt field = 5)

  STP  Xt, Xt2, [Xn] (16-byte pair store)
    ESR_EL1 = 0x000000009600004f   EC=0x25  ISV=0  SAS=0  SSE=0  SRT=0  SF=0  AR=0
    WnR=1  CM=0  S1PTW=0  DFSC=0x0f   FAR_EL1=0x400000000000
    ELR_EL1=0x400001a8  instruction word at ELR = 0xa9001805  (Rt field = 5)

  STUR Xt, [Xn, #1]  (unaligned store)
    ESR_EL1 = 0x000000009600004f   EC=0x25  ISV=0  SAS=0  SSE=0  SRT=0  SF=0  AR=0
    WnR=1  CM=0  S1PTW=0  DFSC=0x0f   FAR_EL1=0x400000000001
    ELR_EL1=0x400001ac  instruction word at ELR = 0xf8001005  (Rt field = 5)

  If ISV=0 the syndrome carries neither the transfer register nor the access size,
  so a write-protect handler must fetch the faulting instruction from ELR_EL1 and
  decode it (or carry a side table keyed by translated-code address). That cost is
  measured as step 2 of the ladder below. Note also that STP has TWO transfer
  registers and writes 16 bytes -- i.e. two guest PTEs -- from one fault.

=== 2. write-protect trap-emulate-reflect cost ladder ===

  -- pattern: 512 consecutive PTE slots in ONE PT page (fork-like)
     control: same loop, writable region (pass 1 / pass 2)     0.41     0.33  ns/store
                                                             pass1    pass2    NET(p2)      cyc
     0  bare permission fault + ERET                         26.86    27.59      27.26       88
     1  + read ESR/FAR, check DFSC + WnR                     27.02    27.43      27.10       87
     2  + fetch faulting insn, decode Rt, read guest reg     29.13    28.32      27.99       90
     3  + apply the store to the guest PT page               29.13    28.32      27.99       90
     4  + rmap lookup PT frame -> shadow L3                  28.40    28.32      27.99       90
     5  + synthesise + store the shadow descriptor           33.85    34.67      34.34      111
     6  + DSB/TLBI VAAE1IS/DSB/ISB                          310.38   231.53     231.20      745
     0' bare permission fault again (drift check)            27.59    26.86      26.53       86
     (increments, pass 2: -0.2 +0.9 +0.0 +0.0 +6.3 +196.9 ns)

  -- pattern: one PTE slot in each of 512 PT pages (scattered)
     control: same loop, writable region (pass 1 / pass 2)     8.63     8.87  ns/store
                                                             pass1    pass2    NET(p2)      cyc
     0  bare permission fault + ERET                        100.02    26.86      17.99       58
     1  + read ESR/FAR, check DFSC + WnR                    103.27    27.43      18.55       60
     2  + fetch faulting insn, decode Rt, read guest reg    107.42    29.22      20.35       66
     3  + apply the store to the guest PT page               28.40    28.40      19.53       63
     4  + rmap lookup PT frame -> shadow L3                  28.56    28.08      19.21       62
     5  + synthesise + store the shadow descriptor           43.38    45.49      36.62      118
     6  + DSB/TLBI VAAE1IS/DSB/ISB                          240.32   277.02     268.15      864
     0' bare permission fault again (drift check)            26.45    26.86      17.99       58
     (increments, pass 2: +0.6 +1.8 -0.8 -0.3 +17.4 +231.5 ns)

=== 3. trap every store, versus unprotect / burst / re-protect / resync ===
  The flip arms pay: 1 shadow-descriptor edit + TLBI to unprotect, N native stores,
  1 edit + TLBI to re-protect, then a full 512-entry re-derivation of the page's
  shadow. The `+TLBI` arm ends with one TLBI VMALLE1IS (needed when any entry was
  MODIFIED); the `noTLBI` arm omits it (legal when every entry was an INSTALL).

       N     M     trap-each     flip+TLBI   flip noTLBI  native floor
                  ns/episode    ns/episode    ns/episode    ns/episode
       1 16384          33.6        1137.8         837.5           0.3
       2  8192          67.9        1184.2         851.9           0.6
       4  4096         136.2        1148.4         801.2           1.8
       8  2048         270.4        1119.7         837.6           3.2
      16  1024         559.6        1082.5         812.0           5.7
      32   512        1086.5        1141.4         829.3          10.4
      64   256        2163.2        1100.6         800.1          23.8
     128   128        4325.5        1033.5         904.6          45.2
     256    64        8620.4        1194.0         927.1          84.6
     512    32       17747.4        1507.8        1296.9         162.8

  per-store:
       N      trap-each      flip+TLBI    flip noTLBI
       1          33.64        1137.76         837.46
       2          33.93         592.08         425.93
       4          34.06         287.09         200.29
       8          33.80         139.96         104.70
      16          34.97          67.65          50.75
      32          33.95          35.67          25.91
      64          33.80          17.20          12.50
     128          33.79           8.07           7.07
     256          33.67           4.66           3.62
     512          34.66           2.94           2.53

  break-even burst length, flip+TLBI  : 
      N = 64  (at N = 32 trapping is still cheaper)
  break-even burst length, flip noTLBI: 
      N = 32  (at N = 16 trapping is still cheaper)

  0 failed experiment(s)
